    {
      "id": "8b02b783-5f48-47b7-97b4-afad4d1cc69f",
      "name": "Build Confirmation Summary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1744,
        3744
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "\n// Build a simple confirmation summary to send via Telegram\nconst vendor = $('Validate & Normalise Fields').item.json.vendor;\nconst amount = $('Validate & Normalise Fields').item.json.amount;\nconst currency = $('Validate & Normalise Fields').item.json.currency;\nconst category = $('Validate & Normalise Fields').item.json.category;\nconst totalWithTax = $('Validate & Normalise Fields').item.json.totalWithTax;\nconst isHighValue = amount > 100;\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    confirmationMessage: `✅ *Expense Logged*\\n\\n*Vendor:* ${vendor}\\n*Amount:* ${currency} ${amount}\\n*Total incl. tax:* ${currency} ${totalWithTax}\\n*Category:* ${category}\\n${isHighValue ? '⚠️ _High-value — flagged for review in Slack._' : ''}\\n\\n_Saved to Notion, Sheets & Airtable._`\n  }\n}];\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "5819c706-a5de-4658-80b2-afb2137412eb",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2768,
        2912
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 876,
        "height": 672,
        "content": "## 🧾 Receipt Scanner – Auto-Extract & Track Expenses\n\n### How it works\nTwo triggers feed the same pipeline. **Email:** Gmail fires on receipt emails — attachments are extracted, PDFs go through text extraction, images straight to GPT-4o-mini vision. **Telegram:** send a photo of a receipt to your bot and it downloads and processes it the same way. GPT-4o-mini extracts structured data (vendor, amount, tax, category, date). Fields are validated and normalised. High-value receipts (>100) are flagged to a Slack channel for review. Every expense is logged to Google Sheets AND Airtable for finance tracking, then written to your Notion Expenses database. A formatted Telegram confirmation closes the loop.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Connect **Gmail OAuth2** to `Gmail Trigger Receipts`.\n2. Connect **Telegram Bot API** to `Telegram Trigger`, `Telegram Get Photo File`, `Send Telegram Confirmation`.\n3. Connect **OpenAI API** to both AI Extract nodes.\n4. Connect **Notion API** → `REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_NOTION_EXPENSES_DATABASE_ID`.\n5. Connect **Google Sheets OAuth2** → `YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID` (create `Expense Log` tab).\n6. Connect **Slack OAuth2** → `YOUR_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID`.\n7. Connect **Airtable PAT** → `YOUR_AIRTABLE_BASE_ID` + `YOUR_AIRTABLE_TABLE_ID`.\n8. Activate both triggers."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3b1e1c99-df05-43c9-a25f-a65287a2166a",
      "name": "Section – Gmail Receipt Intake1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1776,
        2912
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1336,
        "height": 576,
        "content": "## 📧 Gmail Receipt Intake\nFires on new receipt emails. Extracts the attachment binary, checks whether it's a PDF or image, and routes accordingly. PDFs go through text extraction; images are sent directly to GPT-4o-mini vision. No attachment = early exit."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9dda7975-6092-4579-8b47-06a06ca85d46",
      "name": "Section – Telegram Photo Intake1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1744,
        3568
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 856,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## 📱 Telegram Photo Intake\nWhen you send a receipt photo to your Telegram bot, the workflow checks a photo is present, downloads the highest-resolution version, and converts it to base64 for GPT-4o-mini's vision API input."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7b570e44-aa99-43d4-b35c-d419cd7f01f1",
